---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CLAIMS_ACCESS_KEY, isConfigured } from '../data/web3forms';
import '../styles/wholesale.css';

const live = isConfigured(CLAIMS_ACCESS_KEY);
---
<Base title="Wholesale & Fleet — Airborne Dent Repair" description="Wholesale paintless dent, hail, glass and XPEL tint for dealerships, body shops and fleets across DFW and North Texas. Pickup and delivery, free estimates, lifetime PDR warranty." nav="Wholesale" css="wholesale" forms={true}>
<main>

<!-- ============================ HERO ============================ -->
<section class="hero" id="top">
  <div class="hero-panel">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-navy rv">Wholesale &amp; Fleet Accounts</p>
    <h1 class="display h-xl rv rv-d1">Move The Units.<br>Hold The Standard.</h1>
    <p class="lede rv rv-d2">
      Dealerships, body shops and fleet managers send us the vehicles they can't afford to get
      back wrong. Paintless dent and hail repair, glass and XPEL tint — picked up from your lot,
      repaired to a lifetime warranty, and delivered back ready to sell.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row rv rv-d2">
      <a class="btn btn-solid" href="#account">Open a wholesale account <span>&rarr;</span></a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="tel:+16822260543">Call 682-226-0543</a>
    </div>
    <ul class="hero-facts rv rv-d3">
      <li>Pickup &amp; delivery</li>
      <li>Up to 25 vehicles a week</li>
      <li>Free estimates</li>
      <li>Gunter, TX &middot; serving DFW</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="hero-figure">
    <span class="slot-tag hero-slot-tag">Customer vehicle &middot; Airborne Dent Repair</span>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================ MARQUEE ============================ -->
<div class="marquee" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="marquee-track">
    <ul>
      <li>Pickup &amp; Delivery</li>
      <li>Master ARC Certified Technician</li>
      <li>Lifetime PDR Warranty</li>
      <li>Up To 25 Vehicles Per Week</li>
      <li>Veteran Owned &amp; Operated</li>
    </ul>
    <ul>
      <li>Pickup &amp; Delivery</li>
      <li>Master ARC Certified Technician</li>
      <li>Lifetime PDR Warranty</li>
      <li>Up To 25 Vehicles Per Week</li>
      <li>Veteran Owned &amp; Operated</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================ CAPACITY STATS ============================ -->
<div class="stats">
  <div class="stat rv">
    <p class="fig">25<small>Vehicles per week</small></p>
    <p>Our working ceiling, and we mean it as one. We would rather turn down the twenty-sixth
      car than hand you back a rushed one.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="stat rv rv-d1">
    <p class="fig">Lifetime<small>Warranty on PDR</small></p>
    <p>Every paintless repair we perform, for as long as that panel is on the vehicle. It follows
      the car — which matters on the day you sell it.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="stat rv rv-d2">
    <p class="fig">Free<small>Estimates, every unit</small></p>
    <p>Send one car or send a row. Estimates cost nothing, and they come back written the way a
      carrier expects to read them.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="stat rv rv-d3">
    <p class="fig">ARC<small>Master certified</small></p>
    <p>The work is done by a Master ARC certified technician. Not a rotating crew of whoever
      followed the storm into town.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================ WHO WE WORK WITH ============================ -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap sec-head lead">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-navy rv">Accounts We Serve</p>
    <h2 class="display h-lg rv rv-d1">Different Lots. Same Problem.</h2>
    <p class="prose rv rv-d2">
      Everyone below is measured on how fast a vehicle gets back to earning. What changes between
      them is the paperwork, so we handle that differently for each.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
<div class="whos">
  <div class="who rv">
    <p class="n">01</p>
    <h3>Franchise &amp; Independent Dealers</h3>
    <p>Trade-in reconditioning, lot damage, and the hail event that hit forty units overnight.
      Cars come back photograph-ready for the listing.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="who rv rv-d1">
    <p class="n">02</p>
    <h3>Body &amp; Collision Shops</h3>
    <p>Paintless work sublet out so your booth stays on paint. We work to your estimate and your
      cycle time, not ours.</p>
    <span class="chip blocked">Confirm: R&amp;I in-house or sublet</span>
  </div>
  <div class="who rv rv-d2">
    <p class="n">03</p>
    <h3>Fleet &amp; Commercial</h3>
    <p>Service vans, work trucks and company cars. Vehicles rotate through in batches so you are
      never short more than a few at once.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="who rv">
    <p class="n">04</p>
    <h3>Rental &amp; Auction</h3>
    <p>Turn a unit between renters, or clean up a car before it crosses the block. Dings and
      creases are the cheapest money you will ever make back at sale.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="who rv rv-d1">
    <p class="n">05</p>
    <h3>Insurance &amp; Claims</h3>
    <p>Estimates arrive documented and photographed per unit, so a file can be worked without a
      call back to the shop for the detail that was missing.</p>
    <span class="chip blocked">Confirm: estimate platforms &amp; documentation process</span>
  </div>
  <div class="who rv rv-d2">
    <p class="n">06</p>
    <h3>Employers &amp; Property Managers</h3>
    <p>A storm crosses your parking lot and suddenly thirty employee vehicles are damaged.
      That is one conversation with us, not thirty.</p>
    <span class="chip blocked">Confirm: on-site work at customer lots</span>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================ SERVICES ============================ -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap sec-head lead">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-navy rv">Wholesale Services</p>
    <h2 class="display h-lg rv rv-d1">What We Take In.</h2>
  </div>
</section>
<div class="services">
  <a class="svc rv" href="/hail-damage-repair">
    <span class="shot" role="img" aria-label="Hail damage across a black Mercedes-Benz C-Class hood" style="background-image:url('/img/card-hail-damage.jpg')"></span>
    <span class="svc-body">
      <h3>Hail Damage</h3>
      <p>Whole-lot hail events down to a single trade-in. Paintless where the panel allows it,
        which keeps factory paint and keeps the vehicle's history clean.</p>
      <span class="go">See the work <span>&rarr;</span></span>
    </span>
  </a>
  <a class="svc rv rv-d1" href="/paintless-dent-repair">
    <span class="shot" role="img" aria-label="A reflection board reading a door panel during paintless dent repair" style="background-image:url('/img/card-dent-ding.jpg')"></span>
    <span class="svc-body">
      <h3>Dents, Dings &amp; Creases</h3>
      <p>Door dings from the customer lot, transport creases, dolly rash. The repairs that quietly
        cost you money on every appraisal.</p>
      <span class="go">See the work <span>&rarr;</span></span>
    </span>
  </a>
  <a class="svc rv rv-d2" href="/windshield-replacement">
    <span class="slot">
      <span class="slot-tag">Photo needed &mdash; real windshield job</span>
    </span>
    <span class="svc-body">
      <h3>Windshield &amp; Glass</h3>
      <p>Replacement both mobile and in-shop. We can come to the lot, or the unit rides back with
        the rest of the batch.</p>
      <span class="go">See the work <span>&rarr;</span></span>
    </span>
  </a>
  <a class="svc rv rv-d3" href="/window-tint">
    <span class="shot" role="img" aria-label="A tinted pickup in the shop bay" style="background-image:url('/img/card-window-tint.jpg')"></span>
    <span class="svc-body">
      <h3>XPEL Window Tint</h3>
      <p>XPEL exclusively, carrying the manufacturer's warranty. A consistent film across your
        inventory instead of whatever this month's installer had on the shelf.</p>
      <span class="go">See the work <span>&rarr;</span></span>
    </span>
  </a>
</div>

<!-- ============================ HOW THE ACCOUNT RUNS ============================ -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap sec-head lead">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-navy rv">How It Runs</p>
    <h2 class="display h-lg rv rv-d1">Five Steps. You Do One Of Them.</h2>
  </div>
</section>
<div class="steps">
  <div class="step rv">
    <p class="n">01</p>
    <h3>Send The List</h3>
    <p>Call or email with the unit count and where the vehicles are sitting. Year, make and model
      is enough to start.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="step rv rv-d1">
    <p class="n">02</p>
    <h3>We Estimate</h3>
    <p>Free, on your lot or ours. Every unit written up and photographed on its own, so nothing
      has to be guessed at later.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="step rv rv-d2">
    <p class="n">03</p>
    <h3>We Pick Up</h3>
    <p>Pickup and delivery are part of the account. Nobody on your team spends a morning
      shuttling cars.</p>
    <span class="chip blocked">Confirm: minimum units &amp; pickup radius</span>
  </div>
  <div class="step rv rv-d3">
    <p class="n">04</p>
    <h3>We Repair</h3>
    <p>Master ARC certified work, deliberately low volume, lifetime warranty on every paintless
      repair we perform.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="step rv rv-d3">
    <p class="n">05</p>
    <h3>We Deliver Back</h3>
    <p>Vehicles return to your lot with per-unit photo documentation and the invoice.</p>
    <span class="chip blocked">Confirm: billing terms</span>
  </div>
</div>

<figure class="band band-high" style="margin:0">
  <video class="media-video" aria-label="A slow pan across the vehicles parked outside the Airborne Dent Repair shop"
         src="/video/fleet-pan-02.mp4"
         poster="/img/poster-fleet-pan-02.jpg"
         autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="metadata"></video>
  <figcaption class="band-cap">489 Reed Ln, Unit 2 &middot; Gunter, Texas</figcaption>
</figure>

<!-- ============================ CAPACITY, PLAINLY ============================ -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap plain">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-navy rv">Capacity</p>
      <h2 class="display h-md rv rv-d1" style="margin-block:1rem 1.25rem;max-width:20ch">Twenty-Five A Week Is A Choice.</h2>
      <p class="prose rv rv-d2">
        Our founder spent five years running hail operations that moved hundreds of vehicles a
        month. That is long enough to watch what happens to the work when volume is the only thing
        anyone measures — and long enough to decide not to build a shop that way.
      </p>
      <p class="prose rv rv-d2" style="margin-top:1rem">
        So the ceiling is real. If you need three hundred cars done in two weeks, we are not
        your shop and we will tell you that on the phone rather than three weeks in. If you need
        twenty-five done properly, every week, with the same technician's hands on all of them,
        that is exactly what this is.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="rv rv-d1">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Account Terms At A Glance</p>
      <dl class="ledger">
        <div><dt>Working capacity</dt><dd>Up to 25 vehicles / week</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Estimates</dt><dd>Free, every unit</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Turnaround</dt><dd>Quoted with your estimate</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Typical turnaround, single unit</dt><dd class="pending">Confirm</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Pickup &amp; delivery</dt><dd>Offered</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Minimum units for pickup</dt><dd class="pending">Confirm</dd></div>
        <div><dt>PDR warranty</dt><dd>Lifetime</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Tint warranty</dt><dd>XPEL manufacturer's</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Windshield service</dt><dd>Mobile &amp; in-shop</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Wholesale rate structure</dt><dd class="pending">Confirm</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Billing terms</dt><dd class="pending">Confirm</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Certificate of insurance</dt><dd class="pending">Confirm</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="hint" style="font-size:.76rem;color:#7C8173;margin-top:.9rem">
        Rows marked <em>Confirm</em> are deliberately unwritten. They are answers only the owner
        can give, and a guess here is worse than a blank.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================ PROOF ============================ -->
<section style="border-top:1px solid var(--hair)">
  <div class="wrap sec-head">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-navy rv">Proof</p>
    <h2 class="display h-lg rv rv-d1">The Damage Was Real. Now Find It.</h2>
    <p class="prose rv rv-d2">
      Every photograph on this site is a vehicle that came through our bay. Drag the handle.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="ba-feature ba-half rv rv-d1">
      <div class="ba" data-ba style="--split:50%">
        <div class="ba-layer ba-before" style="background-image:url('/img/hail-01-before.jpg')">
          <span class="ba-tag">Before</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ba-layer ba-after" style="background-image:url('/img/hail-01-after.jpg')">
          <span class="ba-tag">After</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ba-handle"></div>
        <input class="ba-range" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="50" step="0.1"
               aria-label="Reveal the repaired vehicle">
      </div>
      <div class="ba-cap">
        <span>Hail damage &mdash; paintless repair, factory paint retained</span>
        <span>Drag &rarr;</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="gallery">
  <figure class="gal rv"><span class="shot" role="img" aria-label="A white Rolls-Royce Dawn in the shop" style="background-image:url('/img/gallery-rolls-royce-dawn.jpg')"></span><figcaption>Rolls-Royce Dawn</figcaption></figure>
  <figure class="gal rv rv-d1"><span class="shot" role="img" aria-label="A black Mercedes-AMG G 63" style="background-image:url('/img/gallery-amg-g63-front.jpg')"></span><figcaption>AMG G 63</figcaption></figure>
  <figure class="gal rv rv-d2"><span class="shot" role="img" aria-label="A black Mercedes-AMG GLE 63" style="background-image:url('/img/gallery-amg-gle63.jpg')"></span><figcaption>AMG GLE 63</figcaption></figure>
  <figure class="gal rv rv-d3"><span class="shot" role="img" aria-label="A matte grey Ram TRX" style="background-image:url('/img/gallery-ram-trx.jpg')"></span><figcaption>Ram TRX</figcaption></figure>
</div>

<!-- ============================ CAT RESPONSE ============================ -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cat">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow rv">Catastrophe Response</p>
        <h2 class="display h-md rv rv-d1" style="margin-block:1rem 1.25rem;max-width:18ch">When The Storm Is Somewhere Else.</h2>
        <p class="prose rv rv-d2">
          Our teams deploy nationally to severe hail events. If you run rooftops outside North
          Texas and one of them takes a hit, the conversation you are already having with us
          does not have to start over with a stranger who followed the storm into town.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="cat-list rv rv-d1">
        <li>Deployment to severe hail events outside our regular service area</li>
        <li>The same certified standard and the same lifetime warranty on the road as at home</li>
        <li>One point of contact across every location, not a new crew per market</li>
        <li>Estimates documented the same way wherever the vehicles are sitting</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================ THE CASE FOR PAINTLESS ============================ -->
<section style="padding-block:0">
  <div class="pdr-case">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow rv">The Case For Paintless</p>
      <h2 class="display h-md rv rv-d1" style="margin-block:1rem 1.25rem;max-width:16ch">Nothing Gets Repainted.</h2>
      <p class="rv rv-d2" style="max-width:46ch">
        Paintless repair works the metal back from behind the panel. No filler, no sanding, no booth,
        and no color match that is close but not quite. The finish that leaves our shop is the one
        the factory sprayed on.
      </p>
      <p class="rv rv-d2" style="max-width:46ch;margin-top:1rem">
        On a unit you are about to retail, that is not a technical detail. It is the difference
        between a car that presents as original and a car a sharp buyer starts asking questions about.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ul class="case-list rv rv-d1">
      <li>
        <strong>Factory finish retained</strong>
        <span>The panel keeps the paint it left the plant with &mdash; no blend, no match, nothing to fade
          out of step with the panel beside it three summers from now.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Nothing waiting on paint</strong>
        <span>No booth to free up and no cure time to schedule around. The constraint on a paintless
          repair is the technician, not the shop's airflow.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The warranty goes with the car</strong>
        <span>Our lifetime warranty covers the repair for as long as that panel is on the vehicle &mdash;
          which means it transfers to whoever buys it off your lot.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>It is not only for hail</strong>
        <span>Door dings, transport creases, dolly rash. If the metal is stretched and the paint is
          still intact, the panel is a candidate. If the paint is broken, we will tell you so.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================ OPEN AN ACCOUNT ============================ -->
<section id="account" style="border-top:1px solid var(--hair)">
  <div class="wrap sec-head">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-navy rv">Open An Account</p>
    <h2 class="display h-lg rv rv-d1">Tell Us What's On The Lot.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap form-spec">
    <div>
      <p class="prose rv">
        Wholesale inquiries go straight to the claims and accounts desk. Use the form &mdash; it
        reaches the same place and gives us the unit count and the lot up front.
      </p>
      <p class="prose rv" style="margin-top:1rem">
        If you have photographs of the vehicles, send them to
        <a href="mailto:Claimsairbornedentrepair@gmail.com?subject=Wholesale%20account%20inquiry">Claimsairbornedentrepair@gmail.com</a>
        once you have submitted &mdash; an accurate estimate starts with being able to see the
        damage, and this form does not take attachments yet.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row rv rv-d1" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="tel:+16822260543">Call 682-226-0543</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <form class="w3f rv rv-d1" data-w3f data-result="account-result"
          data-fallback-email="Claimsairbornedentrepair@gmail.com"
          data-success="Your inquiry is with the claims and accounts desk. We will come back to you on the number you gave us."
          action="https://api.web3forms.com/submit" method="POST" novalidate>
      <input type="hidden" name="access_key" value={CLAIMS_ACCESS_KEY} />
      <input type="hidden" name="subject" value="Wholesale / claims inquiry from the website" />
      <input type="hidden" name="from_name" value="Airborne Dent Repair website" />
      <input class="w3f-hp" type="checkbox" name="botcheck" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true" />

      <div class="w3f-grid two">
        <div class="w3f-field">
          <label for="w-business">Business name <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
          <input id="w-business" name="business_name" type="text" required autocomplete="organization" aria-describedby="w-business-err" />
          <p class="w3f-err" id="w-business-err"></p>
        </div>
        <div class="w3f-field">
          <label for="w-contact">Contact name <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
          <input id="w-contact" name="contact_name" type="text" required autocomplete="name" aria-describedby="w-contact-err" />
          <p class="w3f-err" id="w-contact-err"></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="w3f-grid two">
        <div class="w3f-field">
          <label for="w-phone">Phone <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
          <input id="w-phone" name="phone" type="tel" required autocomplete="tel" aria-describedby="w-phone-err" />
          <p class="w3f-err" id="w-phone-err"></p>
        </div>
        <div class="w3f-field">
          <label for="w-email">Email</label>
          <input id="w-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" aria-describedby="w-email-err" />
          <p class="w3f-err" id="w-email-err"></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <fieldset>
        <legend>Business type</legend>
        <div class="w3f-choices inline">
          <label class="w3f-choice"><input type="radio" name="business_type" value="Dealer" /> Dealer</label>
          <label class="w3f-choice"><input type="radio" name="business_type" value="Body shop" /> Body shop</label>
          <label class="w3f-choice"><input type="radio" name="business_type" value="Fleet" /> Fleet</label>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <div class="w3f-field">
        <label for="w-volume">Approximate monthly volume</label>
        <input id="w-volume" name="monthly_volume" type="number" min="0" step="1" inputmode="numeric"
               placeholder="30" aria-describedby="w-volume-hint" />
        <p class="w3f-hint" id="w-volume-hint">Vehicles per month, roughly. Our working ceiling is 25 a week.</p>
      </div>

      <fieldset>
        <legend>Services needed</legend>
        <div class="w3f-choices">
          <label class="w3f-choice"><input type="checkbox" name="services" value="Hail damage repair" /> Hail damage repair</label>
          <label class="w3f-choice"><input type="checkbox" name="services" value="Dents &amp; door dings" /> Dents &amp; door dings</label>
          <label class="w3f-choice"><input type="checkbox" name="services" value="Windshield &amp; glass" /> Windshield &amp; glass</label>
          <label class="w3f-choice"><input type="checkbox" name="services" value="XPEL tint" /> XPEL tint</label>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <div class="w3f-field">
        <label for="w-message">Anything else we should know</label>
        <textarea id="w-message" name="message" aria-describedby="w-message-hint"></textarea>
        <p class="w3f-hint" id="w-message-hint">Where the vehicles sit, how many are waiting now, and the turnaround you need.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="h-captcha" data-captcha="true"></div>

      <div class="w3f-actions">
        {live
          ? <button class="btn btn-solid" type="submit">Send the inquiry <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></button>
          : <p class="w3f-unconfigured"><strong>This form is not connected yet.</strong> Its Web3Forms access key is still a
              placeholder, so the submit button is deliberately withheld rather than shipping a form that silently goes
              nowhere. Paste the claims key into <code>src/data/web3forms.ts</code>. Until then, call
              <a href="tel:+16822260543">682-226-0543</a> or email
              <a href="mailto:Claimsairbornedentrepair@gmail.com">Claimsairbornedentrepair@gmail.com</a>.</p>}
        <p class="w3f-legal">
          We use what you send here to quote and carry out the work, nothing else. See our
          <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> and <a href="/terms">terms</a>. Photo uploads are not
          available on this form yet &mdash; email them to the accounts desk and we will match them up.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="w3f-result" id="account-result" role="status" aria-live="polite" tabindex="-1" hidden></div>
    </form>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================ CROSS-LINK TO RETAIL ============================ -->
<a class="cross" href="/#retail">
  <p class="eyebrow">Not a business account?</p>
  <h2 class="display h-sm" style="color:var(--ink)">Personal Vehicle &rarr; Retail</h2>
  <p>Free estimate, loaner vehicles available, and we work with your insurance. Same technician,
    same lifetime warranty.</p>
  <span class="go">Go to the retail side <span>&rarr;</span></span>
</a>

<!-- ============================ FINAL CTA ============================ -->
<section class="final">
  <div class="wrap final-grid">
    <div>
